This target has desktop GL linked in, at the GLSL version oops-gl implements

The same three changes `../spaghetti-kart/patches/0001` makes, where the reasoning
is written out, against this title's newer `libultraship`:

- `gfx_sdl2.cpp` includes `SDL2/SDL_opengles2.h` on every Unix it does not name,
  and this target has desktop GL and no GLES headers, so the include fails at
  `GLES2/gl2platform.h`. A `__PROSPERO__` arm goes before the `#else`.
- `glewInit()` has nothing to load: oops-gl is linked into the payload.
- The non-core desktop fragment shader asks for `#version 130`, which oops-gl's
  GLSL front end refuses; it uses nothing past 1.20.

